  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $r\\geq 2$. A number $n$ is $r$-powerful if for every prime $p$ which divides $n$ we have $p^r\\mid n$. Is every large integer the sum of at most $r+1$ many $r$-powerful numbers?",
